<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Al-Andalus (Umayyad province)</h1><p class="st-meta">711 CE – 756 CE · capital Córdoba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Iberia as a province of the Umayyad Caliphate of Damascus, ruled by governors from 711 until Abd al-Rahman I founded an independent emirate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 711 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> crossed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> with a mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> army and defeated the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalete">Guadalete</a>. His superior <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musa-ibn-nusayr">Musa ibn Nusayr</a> followed in 712, and within a few years most of the peninsula had been conquered, often by treaties with local lords such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodemir-visigoth">Theodemir</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tudmir">Tudmir</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">Al-Andalus</a> was governed by walis appointed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, first from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and from around 716 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. Christians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> kept their faith in return for tribute. Raids pushed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</a> was defeated near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> in 732. Tensions between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> erupted in the Berber revolt of 740, after which Syrian troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balj-ibn-bishr">Balj</a> settled in the south.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rival Arab factions fought for power in the 740s and 750s. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> in 750, the Umayyad prince Abd al-Rahman reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 756 and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 711 CE – 756 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:73.85%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>711 CE – 756 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Córdoba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Musa ibn Nusayr, Abd al-Aziz ibn Musa, Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Wilayat al-Andalus, Umayyad Hispania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=734&amp;focus=al-andalus-umayyad-province" aria-label="Al-Andalus (Umayyad province) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4561 815 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Al-Andalus (Umayyad province) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4881 1071L4976 1065M4881 1071L6134 1224M4881 1071L5035 888M4881 1071L488